# Backend Architecture

Source of truth: `docs/architecture/backend.md`, `docs/architecture/workspace-topology.md`.

## Layers (dependency points inward)

```
apps/api, apps/worker          ← thin transport
  → composition/<context>      ← Nest modules (port → adapter wiring)
  → infrastructure/{postgres,redis,messaging}
  → application/<context>      ← @Injectable use cases
  → domain/<context>           ← pure models + repository PORTS
  → shared-kernel-types

platform                       ← capability ports (Cache, Lock, PubSub, UnitOfWork)
```

Bounded contexts are **folders** inside each layer: `identity`, `tenancy`, `authorization`, `audit`, `notifications`.

## Apps (thin)

Controllers/processors only: validate with contracts, map DTO → command, call use cases. No business logic, no TypeORM, no Redis.

```typescript
// apps/api — tenancy controller
@Controller('tenants/:tenantId/invitations')
export class InvitationsController {
  constructor(private readonly inviteMember: InviteMemberUseCase) {}

  @RequirePermission('tenant.members.invite')
  @Post()
  async invite(
    @Param() { tenantId }: TenantIdParamDto,
    @Body() body: InviteMemberInputDto,
  ) {
    return this.inviteMember.execute({
      tenantId,
      email: body.email,
      roleIds: body.roleIds,
      actorUserId: this.currentUser.id,
    })
  }
}
```

## Application

- `@Injectable` use cases only Nest seam allowed
- Own transaction boundaries via `UnitOfWork`
- Own fine-grained authorization
- Depend on **ports** from `domain` / `platform`, never on infrastructure
- Never import `@b2b-saas-starter-kit/contracts`

```typescript
@Injectable()
export class InviteMemberUseCase {
  constructor(
    private readonly uow: UnitOfWork,
    private readonly authz: AuthorizationPort,
    private readonly memberships: MembershipRepository,
  ) {}

  async execute(cmd: InviteMemberCommand) {
    await this.authz.require(cmd.actorUserId, 'tenant.members.invite', {
      tenantId: cmd.tenantId,
    })
    return this.uow.run(async () => {
      const membership = Membership.invite(cmd)
      await this.memberships.save(membership)
      return membership
    })
  }
}
```

## Domain

Pure TypeScript. Repository **ports** live here. No Nest, TypeORM, Redis, or HTTP. See `domain-layer.mdc`.

## Platform

Capability ports only (`CachePort`, `LockPort`, `PubSubPort`, `UnitOfWork`). Adapters live in infrastructure.

## Infrastructure

Implements ports. TypeORM entities + mappers in `infrastructure-postgres`. Redis adapters in `infrastructure-redis`. Never export entities outside this layer.

## Composition

Per-context Nest modules bind ports → adapters and register use cases. Apps import composition modules.

```typescript
@Module({
  providers: [
    InviteMemberUseCase,
    { provide: MembershipRepository, useClass: TypeOrmMembershipRepository },
  ],
  exports: [InviteMemberUseCase],
})
export class TenancyModule {}
```

## Forbidden

- Domain/application importing infrastructure or Nest beyond `@Injectable`
- Application importing `contracts`
- Business logic in controllers
- Cross-context imports of domain internals (use IDs + events)
